{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>The knife.</b> A knife — so called because it 'eats' the flesh, as you say: ״וְחַרְבִּי תֹּאכַל בָּשָׂר״ (Deuteronomy 32), and because it prepares flesh for eating. Another matter: it is called מַאֲכֶלֶת on account of Israel eating the reward of its merit." "<b>And the two of them went together.</b> Abraham, who knew he was going to slaughter his son, went with willingness and joy like Isaac, who was unaware of the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:55.116275170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}